      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Podcast Listener Survey FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a podcast listener survey?\", \"a\": \"A podcast listener survey is a short set of questions a show sends its own audience about the show: which episodes and segments land, what to cover next, and who is listening. Hosts link it from the show notes or read the link on air, then use the answers to plan episodes and pitch sponsors.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a podcast listener survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe your show, its segments, and the decision the answers should settle in a prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>. Emergent builds the survey and the database behind it. Put the link in your show notes, read it out on the next episode, and change any question with another prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should a podcast listener survey ask?\", \"a\": \"Ask about the show first, then about the listener. Which recent episode did you like most? Which segment would you skip? What topic should the show cover next? For a sponsor profile, add what the listener does and what they buy for the hobby the show covers. End with one open question for anything else.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can a podcast listener survey let listeners rank topics for next season?\", \"a\": \"Give listeners 4 to 6 candidate topics and ask them to put the list in order, top choice first. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/ranking'>ranking survey</a> shows which topics come second and third, not only the winner, which helps when a season has room for more than one theme. On a phone, a single pick is quicker to answer than a full ranking.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should a podcast listener survey have?\", \"a\": \"About 8 for a yearly survey, and 1 to 3 for a rating linked from one episode's show notes. Tell listeners the count on air, and put any sponsor profile questions last and make them optional. A survey Emergent builds can show one question per screen, which keeps an 8-question survey readable on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should I share a podcast listener survey?\", \"a\": \"Share it in the episode itself, in the show notes, and in your newsletter if the show has one. Pin it in any listener community the show runs, and leave it open for 2 to 3 weeks for people who listen late. There are no response caps on a survey Emergent builds, even when an old episode picks up new listeners.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a podcast listener survey include a few fun questions?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add one or two near the end: a light question, such as which past guest a listener would invite to dinner, suits an easygoing show and gives the host something to read on air. Keep the rated questions plain and save the jokes for last. A list of <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/funny-questions'>funny survey questions</a> is a good place to borrow from.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I use podcast listener survey results in a sponsor pitch?\", \"a\": \"Lead with the one number that matches the sponsor's customer, such as how many listeners sell their own work, and say how many people answered and in which month. Share totals, never individual answers. With Emergent, every answer sits in a database you own, and a new count for a different sponsor takes one more prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should I run a podcast listener survey?\", \"a\": \"Once a year for the full survey, plus a short rating in the show notes whenever you try a new segment. Run the yearly survey in the same month each time, and keep its questions the same, so this year's numbers line up with last year's. Skip a round if nothing on the show has changed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a podcast listener survey use yes or no questions?\", \"a\": \"Yes, for single checks: would you want a bonus episode, should the mailbag stay, did you hear the last 3 episodes? Each is one tap on a phone and easy to count. Use a scale instead when you want to track a score over time. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/yes-no-questions'>yes no questions survey</a> works well as a quick check between yearly surveys.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
