       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Post Event Survey Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are good post-event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good post event survey questions are short, specific, and about something the person experienced, like a session they sat in or the line at check-in. Use one rating scale throughout so scores compare across sessions. Leave out anything the person could not judge, such as the event budget or the choice of caterer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a post event survey?\", \"a\": \"Describe the event, who attended, and what you want to learn in a prompt. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> drafts the questions, the send time, and the table that stores every answer. Publish it, then share the link by email or on a QR code printed on signs at the exits.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an event feedback form include?\", \"a\": \"An event feedback form needs a few fields besides the questions: the person's role (attendee, speaker, or exhibitor), the sessions they attended, and a checkbox asking whether you may follow up. Those fields let you split answers by group and reply to complaints. Keep the form short enough to finish on a phone.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an event feedback survey be anonymous?\", \"a\": \"Make it anonymous when the questions judge people, and named when you need to follow up. A named event feedback survey lets you call back an unhappy exhibitor or tie each answer to the sessions someone attended. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/church'>church survey</a> that asks about a pastor is a good case for anonymity; feedback on a parish picnic can carry names.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good pre event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Good pre event survey questions ask what people want from the event while you can still plan for it. Ask which topic they most want covered, any dietary or access needs, and which sessions they plan to attend. Their answers set room sizes and catering counts, and give the post event survey something to check against.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should you send after event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Send after event survey questions within a day of the close, while people still remember which sessions they sat through. For a multi-day event, a short survey each evening catches problems you can still fix the next morning. Send one reminder to anyone who has not answered after three days.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some examples of post event survey questions?\", \"a\": \"Five that fit a conference or a trade show: How would you rate the event overall? Which session will you use at work? Was anything hard to find, such as rooms or food? Would you come next year? What one change would you make? For a paid event, add the value question a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/customer-feedback'>customer feedback survey</a> would ask: was the ticket worth the price?\"}, {\"q\": \"Should post event survey questions for attendees differ from those for speakers?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Attendees judge content, logistics, and value for the ticket, while speakers judge the room, the audio setup, and the audience they got. Send each group its own short version, and tag every answer with the group so you can read them apart. Emergent builds every version in one app, with no cap on how many responses come in.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an event feedback survey template you can start from?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Describe your event in a prompt, such as a two-day conference with 30 sessions and 40 exhibitors, and Emergent drafts a starting template: questions, rating scales, and the table behind them. Rename a session, add a question, or split the survey by audience with a follow-up prompt instead of editing each field.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an event satisfaction survey?\", \"a\": \"An event satisfaction survey measures how satisfied people were with one event, through an overall score and a rating for each part. It is shorter than a full post event survey, and repeating it after every event lets you compare scores over time. For a company offsite, keep it apart from an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-satisfaction'>employee satisfaction survey</a>, which asks about the job, not the day.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
